 "scene_id": "09.2",
 "poem": "09",
 "movement": "TEARS, AN ABYSS",
 "title_card": "09 · TEARS, AN ABYSS",
 "set": "harbor_phonebooth",
 "fps": 24,
 "duration": 35.42,
 "lines": "You help me / gather my things to go. / before I go— / I call on my mother. / In tears— / speaking of an abyss / she's never known. / & we talk for years / & re-closet wounds / & re-explain my way of birth / then & even after prayer / what isn't mine, / I still can not give. / we grow old together / with the moon looking / at us—the way / we used to be / as my tears fall between / the creases in / faith— / dancing on my own / maternal ears in tune.",
 "read": "You help me gather my things to go. Before I go, I call on my mother. In tears, speaking of an abyss, she's never known. And we talk for years and we closet wounds and we explain my way of birth then and even after prayer. What isn't mine I still cannot give. We grow old together with the moon looking at us the way we used to be. As my tears fall between the creases and faith, dancing on my own, maternal ears in tune.",
